# quadrant and mirrored both ways. The quadrant sizes are 15x9, 16x9, 17x9,
# 19x11, 20x11 and 23x13 (a room draws from those of its own size).
# Copy this file, then draw. Check it with
#   cargo run -p angel-delve --example content_check -- <your file>
# and add it to its pack's `GREAT` in crates/delve/src/rules/rooms/<pack>.rs.
#
# Marks and rules as room-small.room: `.` floor, `#` block, `~` hazard; the
#   doorway lanes open at their doors (last column of the top row, first column
#   of the last row); the last 3x3 open; every floor tile reachable; 55% floor.
# The bar: a big room is fought in parts: give it two or three places (a
#   colonnade to weave through, a flooded corner to shoot over, an open killing
#   floor in the middle), never one scatter of pillars.
# The Colonnade Court: a row of columns down one side, a sunken pool behind
# them, an open court in the middle.
